{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "```python\ndef is_not_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given integer is a non-prime number.\n    Returns True if n is not prime, False if n is prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return True\n    if n == 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for divisibility from 2 up to the square root of n.\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return True  # Found a divisor, so n is not prime\n    return False # No divisors found, so n is prime\n```"}
