{"task_id": "Mbpp/2", "solution": "```python\ndef similar_elements(list1: list, list2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns a list of unique elements present in both input lists.\n    Uses sets for efficient lookup to find common elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1 = set(list1)\n    shared = []\n    for item in list2:\n        if item in set1:\n            shared.append(item)\n            set1.discard(item) # Ensures only unique shared elements are returned.\n    return shared\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/4", "solution": "```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef heap_queue_largest(numbers: list[int | float], n: int) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n largest numbers from a list and returns them in descending order.\n    Handles edge cases where n is non-positive or larger than the list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n    if n >= len(numbers):\n        return sorted(numbers, reverse=True)\n\n    # heapq.nlargest efficiently finds the n largest elements and returns them in descending order.\n    return heapq.nlargest(n, numbers)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "```python\ndef is_not_prime(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies if a number is not prime.\n    Returns True if the number is not prime, False if it is prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return True\n    if number <= 3:\n        return False\n    if number % 2 == 0 or number % 3 == 0:\n        return True\n\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= number:\n        if number % i == 0 or number % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return True\n        i += 6\n    return False\n```"}
