{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum number of rotations (greater than 0) for a string to return to its original form.\n    It iterates from 1 to string length, checking each rotation.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        rotated_s = s[k:] + s[:k]\n        if rotated_s == s:\n            return k\n    return n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum positive number of rotations for a string to return to its original form.\n    It determines the smallest shift required to match the original string again.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # For a single character string, one rotation returns it to itself.\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Concatenate the string with itself to easily check all rotations.\n    temp = s + s\n    # Iterate through possible rotation counts, starting from 1.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        rotated_s = temp[i : i + n]\n        if rotated_s == s:\n            return i\n\n    # This line should ideally not be reached for non-empty strings,\n    # as a string will always repeat itself after 'n' rotations.\n    return n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(text: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the first and last occurrence of a given character from the string.\n    This function assumes valid string inputs as per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = text.find(char_to_remove)\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return text\n\n    # Remove the first occurrence\n    modified_text = text[:first_idx] + text[first_idx + 1:]\n\n    last_idx = modified_text.rfind(char_to_remove)\n    if last_idx == -1:\n        return modified_text\n\n    # Remove the last occurrence from the modified string\n    return modified_text[:last_idx] + modified_text[last_idx + 1:]\n```"}
