{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a given matrix in ascending order according to the sum of its rows.\n\n    Args:\n        matrix: A list of lists representing the matrix. Each inner list\n                represents a row and contains integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list of lists with its rows sorted in ascending order based on their sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        return []\n\n    # Pair each row with its sum\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        row_sum = sum(row)\n        rows_with_sums.append((row_sum, row))\n\n    # Sort based on the sum (first element of the tuple)\n    rows_with_sums.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract the sorted rows\n    sorted_matrix = [row for _, row in rows_with_sums]\n    return sorted_matrix\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/16", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef text_lowercase_underscore(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if the input string consists of lowercase letter sequences\n    joined by single underscores, or just a single sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The regex pattern specified in the design document.\n    LOWERCASE_UNDERSCORE_PATTERN = r\"^[a-z]+(_[a-z]+)*$\"\n    return bool(re.fullmatch(LOWERCASE_UNDERSCORE_PATTERN, input_string))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\nclass InvalidMatrixError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid matrix input.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> List[List[Union[int, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a 2D numerical matrix in ascending order according to the sum of its rows.\n\n    Args:\n        matrix: A list of lists, where each inner list is a row of numbers (int or float).\n                All inner lists must have the same length and not be empty.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new matrix with rows sorted in ascending order based on their sums.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidMatrixError: If the input matrix is not a valid 2D numerical matrix,\n                            e.g., not a list, contains non-list rows, has ragged rows,\n                            contains non-numeric elements, or contains empty inner lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(matrix, list):\n        raise InvalidMatrixError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    \n    if not matrix: # Handle empty matrix as valid input, returning an empty list.\n        return []\n\n    row_length = None\n    for i, row in enumerate(matrix):\n        if not isinstance(row, list):\n            raise InvalidMatrixError(f\"Row {i} is not a list.\")\n        \n        if not row: # Empty inner list is invalid according to design\n            raise InvalidMatrixError(f\"Row {i} is empty; all rows must have elements.\")\n\n        if row_length is None:\n            row_length = len(row)\n        elif len(row) != row_length:\n            raise InvalidMatrixError(f\"Row {i} has a different length ({len(row)}) than previous rows ({row_length}).\")\n\n        for j, element in enumerate(row):\n            if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n                raise InvalidMatrixError(f\"Element at [{i}][{j}] is not numeric.\")\n\n    # Calculate row sums and sort\n    # The sum() function will handle empty lists gracefully for numeric sums if allowed,\n    # but our validation above ensures rows are not empty.\n    paired_rows = sorted(zip(matrix, [sum(row) for row in matrix]), key=lambda item: item[1])\n    return [row for row, _ in paired_rows]\n```"}
