{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "```python\ndef is_woodall(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is a woodball number.\n    A woodball number's sum of digits equals its product of digits.\"\"\"\n    \n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    abs_number = abs(number)\n    \n    sum_digits = 0\n    product_digits = 1\n    \n    temp_num = abs_number\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        digit = temp_num % 10\n        sum_digits += digit\n        product_digits *= digit\n        temp_num //= 10\n        \n    return sum_digits == product_digits\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "```python\ndef is_woodall(number: int) -> bool:\n    # Woodall numbers are defined as n * 2^n - 1 for non-negative integer n.\n    # This function checks if the input number matches such a definition.\n\n    MAX_N_ITERATIONS = 65 # Upper bound for 'n' to prevent excessively long computations.\n\n    for n in range(MAX_N_ITERATIONS):\n        woodall_candidate = n * (2**n) - 1\n        if woodall_candidate == number:\n            return True\n        if woodall_candidate > number:\n            # If the candidate exceeds the number, further candidates will also exceed it.\n            return False\n    return False # No match found within the iteration limit.\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/17", "solution": "```python\ndef square_perimeter(side_length):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the perimeter of a square given its side length.\n\n    Args:\n        side_length: The length of one side of the square.\n\n    Returns:\n        The perimeter of the square.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If side_length is not a number.\n        ValueError: If side_length is not a positive number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(side_length, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Side length must be a number.\")\n    if side_length <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Side length must be positive.\")\n    return 4 * side_length\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "```python\ndef _reverse_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the digits of an integer, preserving its sign.\n    Numbers ending in zero will have leading zeros removed upon reversal (e.g., 70 becomes 7).\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    sign = -1 if number < 0 else 1\n    abs_number_str = str(abs(number))\n    reversed_abs_number_str = abs_number_str[::-1]\n    reversed_number = int(reversed_abs_number_str) * sign\n    return reversed_number\n\ndef check(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an integer is one less than twice its reverse.\n    This function calls an internal helper to reverse the number.\n    \"\"\"\n    reversed_num = _reverse_number(number)\n    return number == (2 * reversed_num) - 1\n```"}
