{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "```python\ndef check(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    Preserves sign for reversed negative numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    sign = -1 if num < 0 else 1\n    abs_num_str = str(abs(num))\n    reversed_abs_num_str = abs_num_str[::-1]\n    reversed_num = sign * int(reversed_abs_num_str)\n\n    return num == (2 * reversed_num) - 1\n```"}
